<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hall of the Ambassadors (Alhambra)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hall of the Ambassadors (Salón de Embajadores) is the largest room of the Nasrid palaces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhambra">Alhambra</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, inside the Comares Tower, and served as the throne room of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a>. Built under Yusuf I in the fourteenth century, it has a carved wooden dome of thousands of pieces representing the seven heavens of Islamic cosmology, and walls covered in stucco, tilework and inscriptions.</p></div>
